WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.583
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:08.500
- I'm Priscilla and
I'm one of the chalkers

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.080
for @ChalkOfTheDay.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.720
I first got started doing it

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.610
because it was just a way
for me to find an escape

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.533
from the typical routine at MIT.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.620
It really let me with my partner, Jessica,

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.820
to kind of artistically experiment,

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:27.170
and challenge ourselves in ways

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:28.910
that really ended up surprising us.

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:31.400
- I thinks it's nice
because we're all very busy

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.410
and so, setting us
apart an hour every week

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:37.164
to do something artistic
and not think about work

00:00:37.164 --> 00:00:38.163
is really nice.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.583
- I'm Sarah, I'm a senior.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.110
And I've been chalking
since freshman year.

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:50.067
So it's been like six semesters.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.130
Awesome (laughs).

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:58.150
- What is it, it was like
a (imitates shooting).

00:00:58.150 --> 00:00:58.983
- Oh, diagonal?

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.357
Yeah, we should do like, this.

00:01:02.357 --> 00:01:04.370
- I'm Charleen, I'm a senior,

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:06.833
and I study computer science here at MIT.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:12.853
Yeah, maybe like, yeah, yeah.

00:01:12.853 --> 00:01:13.686
- Okay, okay.

00:01:13.686 --> 00:01:15.246
- Yeah, so that's like a good middle size.

00:01:15.246 --> 00:01:16.996
- Nice.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.660
- I'm just looking at pictures of snowflakes.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.220
Words are really powerful,

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:27.760
and so being able to, kind of
convey the meaning of the word

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.810
through the way that you write it,

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:31.453
is kind of interesting to me.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:43.300
- There is a creative process
that I have to engage,

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:44.980
but it's a totally different way

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:47.350
that I approach a math
problem versus the way

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:49.153
that I approach a blank canvas.

00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:51.360
Oh, okay.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.063
- [Charleen] Slightly less the...

00:01:59.653 --> 00:02:01.693
- It puts a smile on people's faces.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:06.573
It spreads a positive message
to people who pass by.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.200
It also, hopefully,

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:13.730
encourages other people
to pursue some form of art

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.723
and to be more creative
in their everyday life.

00:02:15.723 --> 00:02:18.300
(upbeat music)

